.TH CLEAR 1 2026-09-25 "Substrate" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
clear \- clear the terminal screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clear
.RB [ \-x ]
.br
.B clear
.BR \-V | \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B clear
clears the terminal screen and its scrollback buffer by writing fixed
ANSI/VT100 escape sequences to standard output:
.TP
.B ESC [ H
Move the cursor to the home position.
.TP
.B ESC [ 2 J
Erase the whole display.
.TP
.B ESC [ 3 J
Erase the scrollback buffer (an xterm extension that other terminals
ignore).
.PP
No terminfo database is consulted and the
.B TERM
environment variable is not examined; the same sequences are written
for every terminal.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-x
Do not clear the scrollback buffer (omit
.BR "ESC [ 3 J" ).
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An unrecognised argument was given, or writing to standard output
failed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR stty (1),
.BR tty (1),
.BR tty (4),
.BR vt (4)
